CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ first closure keeps its own capture: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ second closure keeps its own capture: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.closure]/1 -- each closure is a distinct object with its own
capture members.  Lambda rework Phase B gives each closure object its own
by-copy capture data members, so a factory returning a fresh capturing lambda
per call yields independent closures (make_adder(3) and make_adder(10) no longer
share capture storage).
